====Isuzu RZ Engine====
* The '''{{vanchor|RZ4E-TC}}''' is a 1.9L direct injection diesel powered, turbo intercooled engine which replaced the 4JK1-TCX found in [[Isuzu D-Max]] and [[Isuzu MU-X]]. The new engine's displacement is 1898cc, 601cc less than the 4JK1-TCX. In addition, the RZ4E-TC generates 150&nbsp;hp at 3600rpm and 258&nbsp;lb.-ft. (340Nm) of torque between 1800rpm to 2600rpm, giving it 16&nbsp;hp and 22&nbsp;lb.-ft. more than 4JK1-TCX. Isuzu has claimed that RZ4E-TC will have 19% better fuel efficiency compared to its predecessor. Bore is 80.0&nbsp;mm and stroke is 94.4&nbsp;mm.
* The '''{{vanchor|RZ4F-TC}}''' is a 2.2L direct injection diesel powered, turbo intercooled engine which replaced the RZ4E-TC found in [[Isuzu D-Max]] and [[Isuzu MU-X]] (only in Thailand by model year 2025). The new engine's displacement is 2164cc, 175cc more than the RZ4E-TC. In addition, the RZ4F-TC generates 163&nbsp;hp at 3600rpm and 295&nbsp;lb.-ft. (400 Nm) of torque between 1800rpm to 2600rpm, giving it 13&nbsp;hp and 37&nbsp;lb.-ft. more than RZ4E-TC. Isuzu has claimed that RZ4F-TC will have 10% better fuel efficiency compared to its predecessor. Bore is 83&nbsp;mm and stroke is 100&nbsp;mm.

===CNG===

====<span class="anchor" id="4HF1-CNG"></span>CNG Engines====
Isuzu developed the first [[Compressed natural gas|Compressed Natural Gas (CNG)]] engine series with low-emissions truck mounted with a clean CNG engine emitting zero black smoke.

* The '''4HF1-CNG''' is a CNG engine of 4.334 L capacity (as based on direct injection diesel engine) with non-contact ignition system. Peak torque is 323 Nm, peak power is {{convert|88|kW|PS|0|abbr=on|order=flip}} at 1,500 rpm. Bore is 115&nbsp;mm, stroke is 108&nbsp;mm.
* The '''4HV1''' is a CNG engine of 4.570 L capacity with non-contact ignition system. Peak torque is 353 Nm, peak power is {{convert|125|kW|PS|0|abbr=on|order=flip}} at 3200 rpm. Bore is 115&nbsp;mm, stroke is 110&nbsp;mm. Application used for NPR300 CNG series.

== Five-cylinder ==

=== Gasoline ===

The [[Isuzu i-Series]] uses General Motors-built inline five-cylinder engines.

*2004–2006 used the General Motors-built [[GM Atlas engine#L52|Vortec 3500 Engine]] with 220&nbsp;hp (164&nbsp;kW) and 225&nbsp;ft·lb (305 N·m) of torque.
*2007–2008 used the General Motors-built [[GM Atlas engine#LLR|Vortec 3700 Engine]] with 242&nbsp;hp (180&nbsp;kW) and 242&nbsp;ft·lb (327 N·m) of torque.

== Six-cylinder ==

=== Gasoline ===

====General Motors====

*From 1989 to 1990 the {{convert|2838|cc|L|1|abbr=on|order=flip}} [[GM 60-Degree V6 engine#LL2|LL2]] V6 with single point fuel injection, producing {{convert|122|hp|kW|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|204|Nm|lb.ft|0|abbr=on}} of torque was used in the first generation Trooper.
*From 1990 to 1992 the {{convert|3128|cc|L|1|abbr=on|order=flip}} [[GM 60-Degree V6 engine#LG6|LG6]] V6 engine with {{convert|122|hp|kW|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|224|Nm|lb.ft|0|abbr=on}} was used in the [[Isuzu Wizard|Isuzu Rodeo]] until replaced with the [[Isuzu]]-built 3.2L '''[[#6VD1|6VD1]]''' engine.
*The 2003–2008 [[Isuzu Ascender]] used the General Motors-built [[GM Atlas engine#LL8|Atlas 4200 Engine]] with 275&nbsp;hp (205&nbsp;kW) and 275&nbsp;ft·lbf (373 N·m) of torque. For the 2007 model year, the engine received an increase to 291&nbsp;hp (217&nbsp;kW) and 277&nbsp;ft·lb (376 N·m) of torque.
*The 1996–2000 [[Isuzu Hombre]] used the General Motors-built [[GM Vortec engine#4300|Vortec 4300 Engine]] with 180&nbsp;hp (134&nbsp;kW) and 245&nbsp;ft·lb (332 N·m) of torque.

====Isuzu V engine====
{{Main|Isuzu V engine}}

The Isuzu '''V engine''' is a family of all-aluminum 75° [[V6]] [[gasoline]] engines ranging from 3.2 to 3.5 liters.

